1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
Hi, I'm Viren Chauhan and I'm building Screenmate.

2
00:00:04,460 --> 00:00:07,700
Applying for jobs means entering the same information into different

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:10,780
websites, then writing answers for each role.

4
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:14,340
Screenmate helps to do that directly on the application page.

5
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:18,660
I built the prototype at the AI Tinkerers Agents Everywhere Hackathon

6
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:22,500
with OpenAI. It placed third globally out of

7
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:26,240
687 projects. I represented Atlanta the only

8
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:29,160
U.S. chapter among the top three.

9
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:33,140
Screenmate uses your saved background to fill forms and draft

10
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:37,120
answers. It checks that changes actually went through

11
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:41,080
while leaving personal decisions and final submissions to

12
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:44,500
you. The next step is testing it with job seekers

13
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:48,200
on real applications, measuring where it saves

14
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:52,140
time, fixing what breaks and understanding what makes people come

15
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:55,800
back. I want to make applying less repetitive

16
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:59,840
while keeping people in control of what they send.
